# Merchant Offer Economics

## Purpose

This document defines the core business formulas used by MerchantLift BI.

MerchantLift BI exists to answer one central question:

> Did the merchant offer create incremental profitable spend, or did it simply subsidize customers who would have purchased anyway?

To answer this, the platform must calculate merchant economics from first principles.

---

## 1. Why Merchant Economics Matter

A merchant-funded offer may look successful if total spend and redemptions increase.

However, high redemptions do not automatically mean the campaign created value.

A campaign can fail economically if:

- customers would have purchased anyway
- reward cost is too high
- merchant margin is too low
- platform fees are too high
- refund-after-reward behavior occurs
- fraud or offer abuse increases
- settlement records do not reconcile

MerchantLift BI therefore measures not just spend, but profitable incremental value.

